 "answer_text": "Found 1 disease record for Marfan syndrome: Marfan syndrome [12]. \n\nMarfan syndrome is an autosomal dominant multisystem connective tissue disease primarily caused by mutations in the FBN1 gene [1]. \n\nClinical Features\n\nMedGen lists these clinical features: Aortic regurgitation [2], Arachnodactyly [3], Astigmatism [4], Ectopia lentis [5], Esotropia [6], Exotropia [7], Pes planus [8], Glaucoma [9], Congestive heart failure [10] and Hypertropia [11]. \n\nDisease Background and Prognosis\n\nAlthough there is currently no radical treatment, early identification, early diagnosis, and early treatment can effectively prolong the life span of patients [1]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Marfan syndrome [12]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Marfan syndrome [13]. Pubmed title: [Latest advances in the diagnosis and treatment of Marfan syndrome] [77]. Pubmed title: What Is Marfan Syndrome [79]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [81]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [83]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Marfan syndrome [14]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Marfan syndrome\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Aortic regurgitation [2]. Medgen clinical_features: Arachnodactyly [3]. Medgen clinical_features: Astigmatism [4]. Medgen clinical_features: Ectopia lentis [5]. Medgen clinical_features: Esotropia [6]. Medgen clinical_features: Exotropia [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Pes planus [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Glaucoma [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Congestive heart failure [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Hypertropia [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Micrognathia [15]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral regurgitation [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral valve prolapse [17]. Medgen clinical_features: Myopia [18]. Medgen clinical_features: Pneumothorax [19]. Medgen clinical_features: Emphysema [20]. Medgen clinical_features: Retinal detachment [21]. Medgen clinical_features: Retrognathia [22]. Medgen clinical_features: Scoliosis [23